['Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Four years ago you invested some money at $10\\%$ interest. You now have $\\$439.23$ in the account. If the interest was compounded yearly, how much did you invest 4 years ago?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Maria has 19 cookies. She decided to give her friend 5 of them, and half of the rest to her family. From the rest, Maria decided to eat 2 cookies. How many cookies will she have left?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: In how many ways can four people line up in a straight line if the youngest person cannot be first in line?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Jake has 3 snakes.  Each of them lays 2 eggs.  Most of the baby snakes sell for $250 but one super rare one costs 4 times as much.  How much did he get from selling the snakes?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: If $f(x)=\\frac{x^5-1}3$, find $f^{-1}(-31/96)$.', "Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: In January, Bill's labrador puppy weighs 40 pounds and his dachshund puppy weighs 12 pounds. Each dog gains 25% of their starting weight over the year. What's the difference in their weight at the end of the year?", 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Joan wants to visit her family who live 480 miles away.  If she drives at a rate of 60 mph and takes a lunch break taking 30 minutes, and 2 bathroom breaks taking 15 minutes each, how many hours did it take her to get there?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Bronson is an apple dealer.  He buys apples from farmers and then transports them to the grocery stores and sells them for profit.  He buys individual apples from farmers at a cost of $12 per bushel, and sells them to the stores at a price of $0.40 per apple.  If each bushel contains 48 apples, then how much profit, in dollars, does he make after selling 100 apples?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: In the human body the digestion of proteins takes place primarily in which two organs?\n\nA. Mouth and stomach\nB. Stomach and small intestine\nC. Liver and gall bladder\nD. Pancreas and large intestine\n\nThe final result is the letter of the correct option.', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: On the 5 by 5 square grid below, each dot is 1 cm from its nearest horizontal and vertical neighbors. What is the product of the value of the area of square $ABCD$ (in cm$^2$) and the value of the perimeter of square $ABCD$ (in cm)? Express your answer in simplest radical form.\n\n[asy]unitsize(1cm);\ndefaultpen(linewidth(0.7));\ndot((0,0));\ndot((0,1));\ndot((0,2));\ndot((0,3));\ndot((0,4));\ndot((1,0));\ndot((1,1));\ndot((1,2));\ndot((1,3));\ndot((1,4));\ndot((2,0));\ndot((2,1));\ndot((2,2));\ndot((2,3));\ndot((2,4));\ndot((3,0));\ndot((3,1));\ndot((3,2));\ndot((3,3));\ndot((3,4));\ndot((4,0));\ndot((4,1));\ndot((4,2));\ndot((4,3));\ndot((4,4));\ndraw((0,3)--(3,4)--(4,1)--(1,0)--cycle);\nlabel("$A$",(3,4),N);\nlabel("$B$",(4,1),E);\nlabel("$C$",(1,0),S);\nlabel("$D$",(0,3),W);\n[/asy]\n\nNote that when we say the grid is 5 by 5 we mean that each row and column contains 5 dots!', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conc