aths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Scout delivers groceries on the weekends.  His base pay is $10.00 an hour.  He also earns a $5.00 tip per customer that he delivers groceries to.  On Saturday he worked 4 hours and delivered groceries to 5 people.  Sunday he worked 5 hours and delivered groceries to 8 people.  How much did he make over the weekend?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: At an auction event, the price of a TV, whose cost was $500, increased by 2/5 times its initial price. The price of a phone, which was $400, also increased by 40% from its original price. If Bethany had taken both items to the auction, calculate the total amount she received for the items after the sale at the auction.', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, th