, 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: How many prime numbers are between 20 and 30?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Following the directions of the arrows, how many different paths are there from $A$ to $C$?\n\n[asy]\npair A,B,C;\nA=(0,0);\nB=(5,0);\nC=(10,0);\ndot(A);\ndot(B);\ndot(C);\nlabel("$A$",A,S);\nlabel("$B$",B,S);\nlabel("$C$",C,S);\ndraw((0,0)--(2.5,1)--(5,0),Arrow);\ndraw((0,0)--(2.5,-1)--(5,0),Arrow);\ndraw(B--(7.5,1)--C,Arrow);\ndraw(B--(7.5,-1)--C,Arrow);\ndraw(A--(5,3)--C,Arrow);\n[/asy]', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Seven identical bowling balls weigh the same as four identical canoes. If three of the canoes weigh a total of 84 pounds, how many pounds does one of the bowling balls weigh?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: A Lamplighter monkey has long arms and can swing from branch to branch at a speed of 10 feet per second.  But when the monkey is frightened, it will run along the branches at a speed of 15 feet per second.  If a Lamplighter monkey runs for 5 seconds to evade a predator, then swings for another 10 seconds to add distance between itself and the predator, how far, in feet, will the monkey travel?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: A patient is receiving treatment through a saline drip which makes 20 drops per minute. If the treatment lasts 2 hours, and every 100 drops equal 5 ml of liquid, how many milliliters of treatment will the patient receive after the 2 hours have passed?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: The American swallow can lift into the air and carry a maximum of 5 pounds of weight, while the European swallow can lift and carry twice the weight as the American swallow.  If there was a flock of 90 swallows, containing twice as many American as European swallows, what is the maximum combined weight the flock can carry?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the